{"name":"Megaman","hex":"#3cbcfc","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"megaman","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A very large or powerful man."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/megaman"}],"entries":[{"title":"Mega Man","blocks":[{"text":"Mega Man is a video game franchise developed and published by Capcom, featuring the eponymous protagonist. The original game was released for the Nintendo Entertainment System in 1987, and spawned a franchise that expanded to over 50 games on multiple systems. As of July 2026, the series had sold a total of 45 million units worldwide.\nMega Man has been popular among gamers and has been reimagined and evolved as a video game character for over 30 years."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mega_Man","wikidata":"Q7565689"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/f/f1/Akira-Kitamura-1991-photo.png/250px-Akira-Kitamura-1991-photo.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/f/f1/Akira-Kitamura-1991-photo.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/f/f1/Akira-Kitamura-1991-photo.png/250px-Akira-Kitamura-1991-photo.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AAkira-Kitamura-1991-photo.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/db/Keiji_Inafune_-_Japan_Expo_13-_2012-0706-_P1410048_%28cropped%29.JPG/500px-Keiji_Inafune_-_Japan_Expo_13-_2012-0706-_P1410048_%28cropped%29.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/db/Keiji_Inafune_-_Japan_Expo_13-_2012-0706-_P1410048_%28cropped%29.JPG/1280px-Keiji_Inafune_-_Japan_Expo_13-_2012-0706-_P1410048_%28cropped%29.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campa